{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"role":"article","title":"Custom State and Traits","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"text":"Carry your own data on entities and in globals, alongside the engine’s closed core.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue"],"anchor":"Custom-State-and-Traits","title":"Custom State and Traits","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/customstateandtraits"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" normally holds one scalar (","type":"text"},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and an item or location carries only the traits the engine knows about (","type":"text"},{"code":"wearable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"surface","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"dark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …). Those closed sets are deliberate: the engine’s behavior branches over a small, readable vocabulary you can audit at a glance. But a game system — a wallet, combat stats, an item’s price — needs to carry data the engine itself never acts on. Custom state and custom traits are the open edges beside that closed core: unlimited declarative data for your rules to read and write, boxed through the same storage the engine already saves and restores.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is the whole idea. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The engine still switches only on the closed core.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Your custom values ride along type-erased and are only ever read by your own rule code."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Rich-Global-state","text":"Rich `@Global` state","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any "},{"code":"Codable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type can be a global. Conform it to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue"},{"type":"text","text":" with an empty conformance — the default implementation JSON-boxes it into the type-erased "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)"},{"type":"text","text":" case, so there’s nothing to hand-pack:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Purse: Codable, Sendable, GlobalValue {","    var coins: Int","    var receipts: [String] = []","}","","struct MyGame: Game {","    @Global var purse = Purse(coins: 10)","    \/\/ …","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Read and write it in rules exactly like a scalar global — it participates in the turn’s commit and in save\/restore through the one world-state funnel:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["lantern.before(.buy) {","    guard purse.coins >= 5 else { try refuse(\"You can't afford it.\") }","    purse.coins -= 5","    try reply(\"Sold. You have \\(purse.coins) coins left.\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The type needs only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" — not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":". The boxed bytes are what participate in the world state’s equality and hashing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Those bytes are the reason to touch a struct global once per rule body rather than field by field. Reading one decodes and writing one encodes, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"purse.coins -= 5"},{"text":" is a decode, a mutate and an encode — fine on its own, but a rule that sets four fields pays for four round trips and, worse, loses an update if a nested expression writes the same global between the read and the write. Read it into a local, mutate the local, and assign it back once:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var wallet = purse","wallet.coins -= 5","wallet.receipts.append(\"lantern\")","purse = wallet"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A custom global is stored as opaque bytes, so if you change its shape, an old save may no longer decode — and a stored value that fails to decode is a "},{"code":"fatalError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not a fall back to the declared default. (The default is only reached when the global’s ID is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"absent"}]},{"type":"text","text":" from the save, which is what happens when you add a whole new global.) Save validation cannot catch it first: it checks only that a "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" case is still a "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" case, and one payload looks like another. So keep custom state structs additive and optional-tolerant — new fields with defaults, and a hand-written "},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps the default when a field won’t decode. Versioned codecs are a later effort."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Note"},{"anchor":"Custom-traits","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Custom traits"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare a typed key once, then use it to declare a custom property inside an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Item { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Location { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trait(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The value is boxed with the same rule as a "},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so a scalar or a whole struct both work:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension TraitKey<Int> { static let price = Self(\"price\") }","extension TraitKey<String> { static let region = Self(\"region\") }","","let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    trait(.price, 5)","}","","let docks = Location {","    name(\"The Docks\")","    trait(.region, \"waterfront\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read it back on the live proxy with the typed subscript, which returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when the trait is absent or stored as a different type:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let price = lantern[.price] ?? 0"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A key declared with a default (","type":"text"},{"code":"TraitKey(\"weight\", default: 1)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") can be read as a non-optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"V","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through ","type":"text"},{"code":"item[default: .weight]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom traits are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"immutable declared facts"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — they never touch the world state. For per-entity state that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"changes","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" during play (an item’s current charge, a creature’s HP), use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keyed however your system needs; traits are for the fixed properties an entity is born with.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Closed core, open edges","anchor":"Closed-core-open-edges"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The engine never switches on a custom trait or a ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" global — it only branches over the closed ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ItemTrait","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/LocationTrait","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" kinds and scalar "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" cases it acts on ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isSurface"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isWearable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dark"},{"type":"text","text":", …). That’s what keeps the engine auditable: every behavior it drives is still visible in a handful of small enums, while your systems get unlimited declarative properties that only your rules interpret."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Worked example","level":2,"anchor":"Worked-example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lighthouse","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" example ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Lighthouse\/"},{"type":"text","text":") keeps two "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":"s — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tideStage"},{"type":"text","text":", bumped by a daemon and read by a room’s live description, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keeperGreeted"},{"type":"text","text":", flipped by a dialogue rule — a compact look at custom state driving prose and branching."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/CustomStateGames.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" builds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShopGame"},{"type":"text","text":": a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purse"},{"type":"text","text":" struct held in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":", a lantern with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trait(.price, 5)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a game-defined "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"buy"},{"type":"text","text":" verb whose rule reads the price and debits the purse — the commerce plugin in miniature. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStateTests"},{"type":"text","text":" boots it and confirms the struct global round-trips through save\/restore, the custom trait reads back through the typed subscript, and absent\/wrong-type reads return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"See-also","text":"See also","type":"heading","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins","type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Global":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/global","type":"topic","title":"Global","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Global","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Global","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Custom game state with the same ergonomics as built-in state:","type":"text"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ItemTrait":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/itemtrait","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ItemTrait","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A single fact about an item, stated inside an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Item { … }"},{"type":"text","text":" block."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ItemTrait"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ItemTrait","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ItemTrait"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","title":"Gnusto","abstract":[{"text":"A Swift engine for writing parser-driven interactive fiction — text adventures in the tradition of Zork and Infocom’s ZIL.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GlobalValue":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Types usable with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":" property wrapper."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GlobalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GlobalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"GlobalValue","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/globalvalue"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/LocationTrait":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LocationTrait","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/locationtrait","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/LocationTrait","title":"LocationTrait","abstract":[{"text":"A single fact about a location, stated inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Location { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LocationTrait","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/StateValue/data(typeName:bytes:)":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"data","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"typeName","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bytes","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4DataV","text":"Data","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"StateValue.data(typeName:bytes:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/statevalue\/data(typename:bytes:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/StateValue":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateValue"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateValue"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A value that can live in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WorldState"},{"type":"text","text":"’s global storage. The scalar cases"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each pair with a dedicated "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GlobalValue"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the type-erased case that carries any other "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" value, so custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state structs and custom traits need no new case of their own."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/statevalue","title":"StateValue","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world."}],"title":"Writing Rules","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Plugins":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/plugins","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Package a reusable game system as an importable unit of verbs and rules."}],"title":"Plugins","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic"}}}